{
  "source": "Curated position overrides — a league-wide role review (30-team agent pass, adversarially verified) layered on top of the Basketball-Reference play-by-play scrape. Fills secondary positions the play-by-play table never measured (only ~230 players qualify) and corrects role-blind adjacency fallbacks (e.g. a small-ball five's second spot is C, not SF). Measured play-by-play primaries stay authoritative; only advanced-page fallback primaries are corrected here. Jul 28 2026: added the curated-* stubs for players with no Basketball-Reference row (overseas returnees, two-way conversions, a traded two-way) — primary from Spotrac's feed position where specific, else the slot they actually play. Aug 17 2026: seven more stubs (the Jul 1 – Aug 5 signings whose sheet row never existed), same rule — feed position where specific, and Plowden's bare \"G\" read as SG. Aug 17 2026 (later): the fifteen stubs that turned out to have real Basketball-Reference ids were rekeyed from curated-* to those ids. Every one of them is an advanced-page fallback primary in positions-2026.json (none has play-by-play shares), so the curated read still wins under the rule above; Ron Harper Jr. is the exception — harpero02 IS measured (89% SF), so his stub key was dropped from positions-2026.json rather than moved here. Aug 26 2026: Georges Niang (niangge01) — a real Basketball-Reference id with no position, bio or rating row, because the 2025-26 scrape never carried him. He sat on an expiring $0 sheet row until Golden State signed him, at which point he became a rostered player the position guard could see. Feed position.",
